1790131046097699	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhxE		item.comment	bn-31iu	{"body":"Implemented TEST-2-07/08 in a new module sections/s2_cancellation_fairness.py (no lines of bn-1fqu's s2_generated_systems.py/tsys.py/Justfile touched). Payload layers cancel{} and fairness[] over a plain tsys system; extension functions reuse tsys.compile_system/enabled/fire/explore/Finding/SplitMix64. TEST-2-07: static ref-integrity + phase-order (request<drain<finalize) + finalize-discharges rules, plus a dynamic rule (no state past a process's last finalize step still holds its obligations, docs/02 §7). TEST-2-08: weak-fairness only — a fair transition must be co-enabled with something (non-vacuity) and never guard-enabled at a dead-end state; strong fairness explicitly out of scope (acyclic-only oracle), documented in BOUNDARIES and README-test.md. 64-seed corpus, 4 structural mutants (100% detected), 8 fixtures (1 per rule + clean control). Both requirements enforced, 0 failures. Annotated docs/19 §2 bullets delivered, ran just traceability (regenerated PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md), then CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 just check: pass (fmt, clippy, test, boundaries, covenant, governance, dossier, lean, test-policy). Committed as 910f115."}	blake3:-6jrWjIuQjqofjA3rK00eh9nvztWR8Hyw48eI31mwLE
